  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is grafana_sync, the checkout directory is nextcloud-grafana.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node 22 stated in .nvmrc, within package.json engines.node ^20 || ^22 || ^24.",
        "  Not stated in node-version in the workflows, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (eslint.config.js), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHPUnit (tests/phpunit.unit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php).",
        " No Stylelint configuration: stylesheets are unchecked, and a mistake in CSS fails silently instead of loudly.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "1 declared package is named nowhere in the checkout: @nextcloud/router.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 264 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0-or-later (package.json, composer.json).",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. With min-version 32 info.xml can state an SPDX id instead.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "versions-agree",
